🔹 1. final — Keyword
Used to declare constants, prevent method overriding, or inheritance.

Use	Description
Final variable	Value cannot be changed once assigned
Final method	Cannot be overridden by subclasses
Final class	Cannot be extended (inherited)

🔹 2. finally — Block
Used in exception handling to execute important cleanup code, runs regardless of exception.

🔹 3. finalize() — Method
Defined in the Object class.

Called by the Garbage Collector before destroying an object.

Used to perform cleanup operations, like closing resources.